Radiolaria genome sequencing has its own page: the
[*Plagiacantha* genome project](../projects/plagiacantha-genome.qmd), a community effort
to build the first radiolarian genome and a model system with it.

### Collaborators

- [**Jeremy Wideman**](https://evocellbio.com/), Arizona State University.
  Organellar genome organization, sequencing, and assembly.
- [**Johana Rotterová**](https://www.microttlab.org/), University of Puerto Rico
  Mayagüez. Molecular diversity of protists, with expertise in ciliates and
  anaerobes, and collection in Puerto Rico.
- [**Leocadio Blanco-Bercial**](https://search.asu.edu/profile/4317967),
  Bermuda Institute of Ocean Sciences and Arizona State University. Radiolarian
  and zooplankton ecology.
- [**Derk Joester**](https://joester.mccormick.northwestern.edu/), Northwestern
  University. Biomineralization and materials characterization.

## The wider community

::: {.logo-block .logo-right}
[![](../images/radiolaria/lifeOfRetaria_logo.png){width=200 fig-alt="Life of Retaria"}](https://thelifeofretaria.github.io/)

::: {.logo-text}
[Life of Retaria](https://thelifeofretaria.github.io/) is a group of early
career researchers organizing the global community of people who work on living
retarians, sharing data and ideas across labs. Anyone working on these organisms
should know about it.
:::
:::

